{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2140-12-18 16:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , one of your transplant team doctors. I understand you came in today with nausea and vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2140-12-18 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, Doctor. I woke up this morning feeling really nauseous and threw up a couple times. But it’s better now—I’m actually hungry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2140-12-18 16:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear the nausea is improving. You mentioned some pain over your graft site when you arrived—how’s that feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2140-12-18 16:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s not really painful now. Just a little fullness. But I haven’t had a bowel movement in three days, and I haven’t passed gas either."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2140-12-18 16:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that’s important. We’ve ordered a KUB X-ray and a renal ultrasound to check things out. Constipation can definitely cause discomfort, especially after surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2140-12-18 16:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been trying to stay regular. I’m on senna and Colace. But nothing’s moving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2140-12-18 16:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll help with that. The imaging will give us a clearer picture. We also need to check your kidney function and make sure your transplant is doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your KUB came back. It shows moderate fecal loading in the colon—so yes, you’re quite constipated. But no blockage, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s probably why I’ve been feeling so bloated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re going to start with milk of magnesia. If that doesn’t work, we may need an enema. We want to avoid straining or discomfort near your graft site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my kidney? Is it okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ultrasound shows your transplanted kidneys are working well—your urine output is good and your creatinine is around 1.4, which is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But the report mentioned something about fluid around the kidney?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, there’s a large fluid collection around the transplant site. It’s been there since your last admission. We’re watching it closely, but it hasn’t changed much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it dangerous? Could it get infected?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring for that. You’re already on micafungin through your PICC line to prevent infection, especially since you had Candida before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, I remember. And my WBC is low again, isn’t it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your white count is between 2.3 and 3.0. It’s low, likely due to your anti-rejection meds. We’ve reduced your Valcyte dose to help protect your bone marrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that increase my risk of infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2140-12-18 17:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re balancing risks. Lowering Valcyte helps your counts, but we’re keeping you on other protections like micafungin and monitoring closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2140-12-19 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How did you sleep? Any bowel movement yet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2140-12-19 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not yet. I took the milk of magnesia, but nothing happened."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2140-12-19 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll try a soap suds enema today. If that doesn’t work, we’ll add lactulose. We really want to get things moving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2140-12-19 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The enema helped a little, but not fully. We’re starting lactulose—30 mL daily. That should help soften things up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2140-12-19 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope so. My belly feels so tight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2140-12-19 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’re also watching your blood pressure. It’s been a bit low, so we’ve reduced your amlodipine and carvedilol doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2140-12-19 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling a little dizzy when I stand up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2140-12-19 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be from the lower BP. We’ll keep an eye on it. Also, your Prograf level was high yesterday—16.6."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2140-12-19 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "High? I thought higher was better for preventing rejection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2140-12-19 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. Too high can be toxic—cause kidney issues or tremors. We lowered your dose to 3 mg twice daily. Today’s level is 11.2, which is much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2140-12-19 10:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. So we’re aiming for a sweet spot?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2140-12-19 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We want enough to prevent rejection, but not so much that it harms you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2140-12-19 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—your labs show your creatinine is stable at 1.2, and you passed three stools after the lactulose. Your constipation is resolving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2140-12-19 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2140-12-19 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If things keep going this well, probably tomorrow. We’ll remove the wound VAC today—the site is small and clean."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2140-12-19 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just a regular dressing after that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2140-12-19 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, saline damp-to-dry dressing once a day. You can shower, but no baths or swimming."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge today. Your condition is stable—clear mind, walking on your own, eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my meds? Anything changed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Prograf is now 3 mg twice daily, carvedilol is 12.5 mg twice daily, and Valcyte is 450 mg daily. You’ll also take lactulose as needed for constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the micafungin through the PICC?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue that daily until the end date on the prescription. Home health will help with that and your dressing changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call the clinic if you have fever, nausea, vomiting, constipation, redness at the incision, or decreased urine output. Check your weight daily—let us know if you gain 3 pounds in a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And labs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Twice weekly. Don’t take your Prograf until after your blood is drawn. Bring the dose with you so you can take it right after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you, Doctor. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2140-12-20 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. We’ll see you in follow-up. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2140-12-18 16:31:00",
    "admission_end": "2140-12-20 15:35:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient was admitted 30 days after a deceased donor pediatric en bloc kidney transplant for nausea, vomiting, and constipation. He had not passed stool or gas in three days, though his graft function remained stable with a creatinine of 1.2–1.4. Imaging confirmed moderate fecal loading without obstruction and showed an interval increase in pelvic fullness of both transplanted kidneys with a stable complex perinephric fluid collection. Constipation was managed with milk of magnesia, enemas, and lactulose, leading to resolution. His Prograf level was initially elevated at 16.6, prompting a dose reduction to 3 mg twice daily, with subsequent improvement to 11.2. Due to low white blood cell count, Valcyte was reduced, and antihypertensives were adjusted for low blood pressure. The wound VAC was discontinued as the incision healed. He was discharged home with home health support on adjusted immunosuppression, continued micafungin, and instructions for ongoing monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "End stage renal disease"
    ]
  }
}
